cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Linked-Intent Development (LID)"
message: "If you use LID or its plugins, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Szmajda
    given-names: Jess
abstract: >-
  Linked-Intent Development (LID) is a structured design-before-code
  methodology for agentic coding that keeps intent and code coherent through a
  traceable arrow: high-level design to low-level design to EARS specifications
  to tests to code.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jszmajda/lid"
url: "https://linked-intent.dev"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agentic-coding
  - spec-driven-development
  - claude-code
  - linked-intent-development
  - methodology
  - ears
